3T03:24:29Z","body":"@benvanik: Looking into this with some printf debugging in VM, I find something suspicious:\r\n\r\n```\r\n[module.forward+00000000]    <block>\r\n[module.forward+00000001]    %i0 = vm.const.i32 30720  // 0x00007800\r\n\r\n// Lots of VM dispatch happening, till the end...\r\n\r\n[module.forward+00020348]    %i0 = vm.call.varadic @hal.fence.await(%i45(4294967295), %r1(!hal.fence/0x0x55b33dba66b0))\r\n[module.forward+0002035E]    vm.cond_br %i0(0), ^000203A0(), ^0002036E()\r\n[vm]  current condition: 30720\r\n[vm]  true pc: 132000\r\n[vm]  false pc: 131950\r\n[module.forward+000203A1]    vm.fail %i0(0), \"failed to wait on timepoint\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe call to `@hal.fence.await` [succeeds with `rets->i0 = 0`](https://github.com/openxla/iree/blob/c31c8a0/runtime/src/iree/modules/hal/module.c#L1338). The following `vm.cond_br` are actually not seeing `%i0` being 0; rather it's reading the previous `%i0` definition?\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1480549309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/comments/1480551057","html_url":"https://github.com/iree-org/iree/issues/12670#issuecomment-1480551057","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/iree-org/iree/issues/12670","id":1480551057,"node_id":"IC_kwDODGgK6M5YP2qR","user":{"login":"antiagainst","id":487928,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4NzkyOA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/487928?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst","html_url":"https://github.com/antiagainst","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antiagainst/gists{/gist_id}","starred_u